# ============================================================
# Question Bank Seed Script — v3 (varied aptitude set)
# File: seed_questions.py (run from hireview-backend/ directory)
#
# v3 change: the v2 aptitude set was template-generated with only the
# numbers swapped per question (same sentence, same topic, over and
# over) — that reads as repetitive/low-effort to a candidate who has
# seen even one free mock test online. This version keeps the same
# "correct by construction" guarantee (every answer is computed by
# the same code that writes the question, in gen_aptitude.py, so
# there is no hand-arithmetic to get wrong) but generates from
# multiple distinct sentence templates per topic — different framing,
# named people, shops/items, currencies — and de-duplicates prompts.
# 130 aptitude questions across 13 topics (10 each), including 3 new
# topics not in v2: compound_interest, ages, permutations_and_combinations.
#
# Counts: 130 aptitude, 30 coding, 28 interview.
#
# Coding and interview sets are unchanged from v2 (already
# hand-verified — see provenance note below) and are not touched here.
#
# Provenance / verification:
#   - Aptitude: generated by gen_aptitude.py, answer computed by the
#     same formula that renders the question text, then de-duplicated
#     and spot-checked by hand (see conversation for a 12-question sample check).
#   - Coding: every one of the 30 problems has a hand-written C
#     reference solution that was compiled with gcc and RUN against
#     every test case (93 total test cases across all 30 problems) —
#     output diffed against expected_output before being included here.
#   - Interview: no "right answer" to verify; each has guidance_notes
#     for later feedback-scoring use (not shown to the candidate).
#
# 30 coding problems is short of the "100 coding" target in the
# original brief — the other 70 need the same compile+run verification
# before they can ship with the same guarantee. Flagged to AP rather
# than padded with unverified content.
#
# Run once with: python seed_questions.py
# To re-seed with this new aptitude set, delete existing question_bank
# rows first (this script skips insertion if the table already has rows).
# ============================================================

import json
from models.database import SessionLocal, QuestionBank, CodingTestCase, init_db


def seed():
    init_db()
    db = SessionLocal()

    if db.query(QuestionBank).count() > 0:
        print("question_bank already has rows — skipping seed (delete rows manually to re-seed).")
        db.close()
        return

